{
  "id": "COMPOUND:14379 - PROTEIN:6311",
  "verbalization": "Efavirenz is shown to have a target relationship with LoVo, a cancer cell line, through multiple pathways. Each of these pathways links efavirenz to LoVo, which in turn is targeted by different compounds, all of which ultimately lead to a common target: Histone deacetylase 5. The evidence suggests that efavirenz may exert its biological effects by interacting with LoVo cells, which are then targeted by various compounds that share a common downstream effect on Histone deacetylase 5. This indicates that Histone deacetylase 5 may be a key mediator in the mechanism by which these compounds affect LoVo cells. The consistent presence of Histone deacetylase 5 as a target across different pathways supports the idea that it plays a central role in the cellular response to these compounds. The evidence is robust and suggests a clear, interconnected pathway from efavirenz to LoVo to Histone deacetylase 5, though further experimental validation would be needed to confirm the exact mechanism of action.",
